  "gotchas": [
    "Auth: one token server for both environments — the docs' Multi-Environment Integrations example sends either environment's credentials to https://idp.flutterwave.com/realms/flutterwave/protocol/openid-connect/token, and Authentication says \"This process applies to both the sandbox and production environments. Make sure to use the correct credentials for each environment to obtain a valid token.\" \"Each token is valid for **10 minutes**\"; \"We recommend refreshing the token at least one minute before it expires.\" Cache the token. Sandbox: \"We archive your test data after 30 days.\"",
    "Headers: X-Trace-Id is optional on this GET (the headers guide lists it under 'Optional API Headers'; \"It must be a string using only alphanumeric ASCII characters.\", 12-255 characters). The API reference documents no X-Idempotency-Key for this endpoint.",
    "Pay with bank transfer reconciliation: Docs (Pay With Bank Transfer): \"track all the payments made into a virtual account by [querying the charge list](/reference/charges_list) using the virtual account's ID.\" → GET /charges?virtual_account_id=van_…",
    "from / to are ISO 8601 date-times (format date-time, e.g. 2025-04-21T10:55:16Z). status filter: succeeded, pending, failed, voided.",
    "Pagination: page ≥ 1 (default 1, most recent first), size 10-50 (default 10); read meta.page_info.total_pages. The API reference caps some list responses at 10 items (maxItems 10) although size goes up to 50: always paginate. The API reference caps data at 10 items (maxItems 10) although size goes up to 50.",
    "Errors: {\"status\":\"failed\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\",\"validation_errors\"}}; error.code is a string and 400s carry validation_errors[{field_name,message}]. Besides the generic codes (10400 REQUEST_NOT_VALID, 10401, 10403 FORBIDDEN, 10404 RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND, 10409 RESOURCE_CONFLICT, 10422 UNPROCESSABLE, 10500) the error table documents these for this endpoint: 701500 INVALID_PAGINATION_TYPE. Branch on error.type / error.code, not on the HTTP status alone. Docs (Errors): \"The current limit is 500 API requests per minute.\" A 429 can come back as a non-JSON page (\"HTML error pages such as `Cloudflare 1015 responses`\"): parse error bodies defensively and back off exponentially with jitter."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Token URL: the PHP sample of Authentication uses https://keycloak.dev-flutterwave.com/realms/flutterwave/protocol/openid-connect/token; its curl and JavaScript samples and the Multi-Environment example use https://idp.flutterwave.com/realms/flutterwave/protocol/openid-connect/token, which this spec follows."
